Wait, maybe the simplest robust fix: Keep build-time injection AND add runtime override. Then it works regardless. But the user might be confused why they have to set `ADMIN_SHOW...` vs `VITE_SHOW...`. We document deploy.env only. Build-time is internal. Fine.

Would runtime config alone fix the user's current issue? If their browser has the new bundle (it does), and we add runtime config, the deployed `runtime-config.js` would be loaded. But they need to reload. The bundle changes (index html adds script) and new release. They must refresh. But after deploy, with no-cache index, okay.

