Maybe we should implement runtime only and remove build-time. Let's decide based on architecture: The design explicitly says step 2 injects build-time constants. But the user is unhappy with build-time. Runtime is more flexible. Could implement both, with runtime taking precedence. The deploy engine config is the single source, setting both build-time and runtime so no matter how the app is served, it matches. Good.

