parts.text:
Great. Now write a Playwright script to load the admin portal, mock auth and API, and check whether "Snapshot export checklist" is visible. Need admin credentials? We'll inject localStorage user and intercept API.

Let's inspect the localStorage key and auth guard. Key `PAYMENT_GATEWAY:ADMIN:USER`. Set user state with token + userInfo. authority map with `security:read` true and maybe all others? The layout might make API calls; intercept all `/api/**` with generic 200. But specific dashboard endpoints need proper shape. `api.get(urlsMap.dashboardOverview)` -> `/api/v1/admin/stats/overview?period=24h`. Response handled: `response.data?.data ?? response.data ?? {}`. So return `{ data: {...} }` or direct object. We'll return `{ data: { period:'24h', since:'...', attemptsByState:{}, volumeByState:{}, attemptsTotal:0, ... } }`. However axios with fetch adapter returns response.data as the parsed JSON. If we return `{data: {...}}`, then `response.data?.data` is the object. Good. For recent activity, return `{data:{recentActivity:[]}}`.

Other API calls: layout maybe `/api/v1/admin/auth/me` or options; intercept and return `{data:{}}`. Need avoid 401 causing logout. Since all intercepted return 200, fine.

Set `authoritiesMap` with all keys? For the dashboard route no required. But layout nav filtering may call `hasOneOfAuthorities` with undefined for many, fine. The `Recent privileged activity` card requires `security:read`; if we want to include/exclude, not needed for snapshot checklist. We can set `security:read: true`.

The login guard: `isAuthenticated` returns token && userInfo. Good. Also maybe router guard checks route authorities; Dashboard none. Good.

We'll load `http://127.0.0.1:8443/dashboard`. Need ignore HTTPS errors? It's HTTP (ADMIN_SSL false). Use `http://127.0.0.1:8443`.

Playwright script:
```
const { chromium } = require('playwright');
const browser = await chromium.launch();
const ctx = await browser.newContext();
await ctx.addInitScript(() => {
  localStorage.setItem('PAYMENT_GATEWAY:ADMIN:USER', JSON.stringify({ token:'test', refreshToken:null, userInfo:{ id:'1', name:'Tester', username:'tester', role:'GATEWAY_ADMIN', email:null, phone:null, authoritiesMap:{'security:read':true}, isMaker:false, isChecker:false }}));
});
await ctx.route('**/api/**', async route => {
  const url = route.request().url();
  if (url.includes('/stats/overview')) return route.fulfill({status:200, contentType:'application/json', body: JSON.stringify({data:{...}})});
  if (url.includes('/stats/recent-activity')) return route.fulfill({status:200, ..., body: JSON.stringify({data:{recentActivity:[]}})});
  return route.fulfill({status:200, contentType:'application/json', body:'{"data":{}}'});
});
const page = await ctx.newPage();
await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:8443/dashboard', {waitUntil:'networkidle'});
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
const text = await page.locator('body').innerText();
console.log(text.includes('Snapshot export checklist'));
console.log(text.slice(0,1000));
```
Potential issue: The app may call `/api/v1/admin/options/...` and layout may fail but fine. Also the page might show login if localStorage init script runs before app. `addInitScript` runs before page scripts on every navigation. Good.

Also the dashboard page may require `overview` shape with methods. `stats()` computed likely handles missing. Let's check `MiniStats` expects array. Fine.

Also `useLocale` requires vuetify; fine.

Let's write and run.

