admin-front/src/content/guide/booksPart2.ts:235:                "bodyEn": "The `/kyb` workspace is the document-level review queue. It is not a second join-request decision screen: the seven-point checklist, screening context and final four-eyes decision remain on `/join-requests/:id`.\n\n**Queue scope.** The queue shows documents for submitted/active onboarding and active merchants. Documents that belong only to a `DRAFT` join request are excluded from reviewer queues (Edge Case 116). Each row shows the merchant, document type, original file, status, antivirus status, expiry state, duplicate count, related join request/SLA, uploader and reviewer.\n\n**Safe review order.** 1. Confirm `av_status = CLEAN`. A `PENDING` or `INFECTED` file cannot be opened or accepted. 2. Open the secure preview and verify the file is genuine, legible and of the declared type. 3. Compare the legal name, registration number, tax certificate and expiry with the merchant profile. 4. For a `BANK_LETTER`, verify the IBAN/account holder belongs to the merchant legal entity. 5. Read the required-document readiness panel before approving the broader join request. 6. Record the document decision and a clear note.\n\n**Duplicate documents.** A duplicate is the same `sha256` hash under an unrelated merchant, not merely the same file name. A duplicate does not block automatically: it raises a warning and requires written justification before acceptance. Repeated reuse across multiple merchants can open an AML case. Never ignore a duplicate because the preview looks clean; investigate the linked merchant and join request first.\n\n**Expiry and replacements.** A document within 30 days of expiry is `DUE_SOON`; after the date it is `EXPIRED` and cannot be accepted as current evidence. Request a replacement when the document belongs to an open join request: the document is rejected, the join request moves to `INFO_REQUESTED`, and the SLA pauses. For an active merchant, request periodic re-verification instead. A replacement is always a new `kyb_documents` row; the platform never overwrites the old file.\n\n**Access and audit.** Document bytes are encrypted at rest and list/detail APIs never expose ciphertext. Every preview, review, replacement request and automatic expiry is written to `audit_log`. Merchant messages use neutral KYB wording and never expose AML, sanctions, PEP or watchlist details.",
