Nested relation filters work with `setPath`, e.g., `attempt.merchant.tradeName`. Good.

Now implement helper module for worker. Let's create file. Need types for status. We can use string unions.

Let's write `core-back/engine/workers/GatewayInquirySchedules.ts`:
```
import type { PrismaLike, Tx } from "../db/ports";
type Status = ...;
type Row = {...};
const delegate = (db) => (db as any).gatewayInquirySchedule;
const ACTIVE = ["SCHEDULED","RUNNING","RETRYING"] as const;
export const findActiveGatewayInquiry = async (db, attemptId) => { ... }
export const markGatewayInquiryRunning = async (db, scheduleId, at) => { ... } // no-op if no delegate
export const updateGatewayInquiry = async (db, scheduleId, patch) => { ... }
export const reconcileGatewayInquiries = async (db, now) => { ... }
```
For reconcile:
```
const model = delegate(db); if (!model?.findMany) return;
const open = await model.findMany({ where:{status:{in:ACTIVE}}, select:{id:true,status:true,attempt:{select:{status:true,terminalAt:true,nextCheckAt:true}}} });
for (const row of open) {
  const terminal = Boolean(row.attempt?.terminalAt) || ["SUCCEEDED","FAILED","EXPIRED","CANCELLED","BLOCKED"].includes(row.attempt?.status);
  if (terminal) await model.update({where:{id}, data:{status:"COMPLETED", completedAt: now, nextRunAt: now, lastResult: row.attempt.status}});
  else if (!row.attempt?.nextCheckAt && row.status !== "RUNNING") await model.update({status:"EXPIRED"...});
}
```
But if schedule status RUNNING and nextCheckAt null? During worker inquiry, nextCheckAt remains previous value; not null unless poll window expired. If expired, worker will update. Reconcile could mark EXPIRED. We skip RUNNING to avoid race.
